Operational Key Performance Indicators (KPIs) provide measurable insight into Azure service quality and infrastructure health.

A typical operational dashboard tracks:

* Service uptime
* MTTR
* Incident count
* Backup success rate
* CPU utilization
* Storage consumption
* Security alerts
* Monthly cloud spending

# Real-Life Example:
For example, operations managers review KPI dashboards weekly to evaluate whether service-level objectives are being achieved.

# Real-Life Use Case:
A real-life use case is enterprise operations centers monitoring production environments continuously to maintain service reliability.

KPIs transform operational data into actionable business insights.
